From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iscle <albertiscle9@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:07:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Android.bp: Make rutabaga_gfx available to the platform

crosvm's devices crate depends on it, and Qualcomm's qcrosvm is a platform
binary built on that crate.

Change-Id: I3543abf6850f49691b1eac0714fce78e8618bd36
---
 Android.bp                                    |  5 ++-
 third_party/mesa3d/src/magma/Android.bp       | 35 +++++++++++++++----
 third_party/mesa3d/src/util/rust/Android.bp   |  5 ++-
 .../mesa3d/src/virtio/protocols/Android.bp    |  5 ++-
 .../src/virtio/virtgpu_kumquat/Android.bp     |  5 ++-
 5 files changed, 44 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index 5d2a3c6..4ad93ff 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -58,7 +58,10 @@ rust_library {
         "libzerocopy",
     ],
     proc_macros: ["libremain"],
-    apex_available: ["com.android.virt"],
+    apex_available: [
+        "//apex_available:platform",
+        "com.android.virt",
+    ],
     cfgs: [
         "fence_passing_option1",
         "gfxstream_unstable",
